THE CASE FOR FAIL:
SRC_003 replaces Boolean attack with a bounded semiring of defense potentials and computes acceptance as a least fixed point accumulating defense-path potential. The problem requires preserving the validity of every committed root as a root (root status must not depend on being defended). By defining acceptance via accumulated defense potential from committed roots, SRC_003 makes committed-root acceptance contingent on the existence of defense paths, so a committed root with no incoming defense path can receive a non-top potential and fail acceptance. This changes the meaning of attack from defeat to cost and fails to preserve committed-root validity. The target concedes the grounded extension may not be preserved as a special case unless the identity element is chosen carefully, i.e., the proposal does not itself guarantee it.

